# Migration Ground Rules

Source of truth: `source-app/` (Flutter + FastAPI + PostgreSQL). Never edit `source-app/`.
Target: `new-app/` (React + TypeScript + Node/Express + SQL Server).

## Hard rules

1. Never guess. If something is not in `source-app/` or `docs/`, write `Unknown — needs verification` and stop.
2. Never simplify or drop business logic, validation, or calculations found in `source-app/`.
3. One module at a time. Do not start a new module until the current one is verified PASS.
4. Every module follows: Analyze → Document → Verify → Plan → Design → Implement → Test → Compare → Review → Approve → Continue.
5. Before writing code for a module, read the relevant `docs/` section and the matching files in `source-app/` — do not rely on earlier chat memory.
6. After implementing, produce a Legacy vs New PASS/FAIL table before calling anything done.
7. Update `docs/00_MASTER_CHECKLIST.md` status (⬜ → 🟡 → ✅) after each completed step.
8. Never rename database columns unless explicitly approved.
9. Never remove UI controls.
10. Never remove validations.
11. Never merge workflows.
12. Never replace business rules with assumptions.
13. Every implementation must reference the source code.
14. Every response must include code references.
15. Every implementation must update documentation.
16. Every implementation must generate tests.
17. Every implementation must include rollback notes.

## Done gate (objective evidence — not confidence scores)

Do not claim a module or task is done unless all of the following are true:

- All documented fields for the scope are implemented (or listed as Unknown).
- All documented API endpoints for the scope are implemented (or listed as Unknown).
- All tests written for the scope pass.
- Legacy vs New comparison shows no known mismatches.
- Any remaining unknowns are explicitly listed for the user.

If any item fails, stop and report. Do not continue to another module.
